  },
  {
   "text": "Here's why. Every step multiplies $x$ by the same factor.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "f1",
     "tex": [
      "x_{\\text{new}}",
      "=",
      "x - \\eta\\cdot 2x"
     ],
     "size": 96,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.6
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "f2",
     "tex": [
      "=",
      "(1 - 2\\eta)",
      "\\,x"
     ],
     "size": 96,
     "next_to": "f1",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.6,
     "colors": {
      "1": "yellow"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If that factor has size above 1, each step makes things worse. That happens for every $\\eta > 1$.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "cond",
     "tex": [
      "|1 - 2\\eta| < 1",
      "\\iff",
      "0 < \\eta < 1"
     ],
     "size": 66,
     "next_to": "f2",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 1.0,
     "colors": {
      "2": "green"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bc",
     "around": "cond",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And $\\eta = 0.5$ makes the factor exactly zero: one step lands right at the bottom.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "half",
     "tex": [
      "\\eta = 0.5",
      "\\Rightarrow",
      "x_{\\text{new}} = 0"
     ],
     "size": 72,
     "next_to": "cond",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.9,
     "colors": {
      "0": "teal"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "For any quadratic valley the limit is $\\eta < 2/f''$: the sharper the curve, the smaller the step must be.",
   "do": [
